 - FINDING: the worker request carries only Go/tool paths, and the process executor starts `GOROOT/bin/go` without a bound content identity or descendant observation. A replacement/execute/restore probe produced equal pre/post launcher digests while an executable outside `GOROOT/pkg/tool/<host>` ran; `ProcessResult.started` still reported one.
 - FINDING: worker-domain teardown is not fail-closed. Windows `CloseHandle` failure is swallowed and the Job Object handle is discarded; macOS group-kill failures can likewise fall back to killing only the worker without proving the complete domain joined.
 - VERDICT: changes requested; route `to-dev`. Rework must bind the complete mutable worker TCB, bind/recheck Go and tool identities at the execution boundary with a real outside-tool negative, and propagate/verify complete-domain teardown failures. Evidence: `TASK-260720-2g21eg_review-verdict.md`.
